RF.put("questb:b68",{"8628":{"id":8628,"t":"Avenger's Crown","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'lor's Diadem Emperor Vek'lor in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Rebirth Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nAvenger's Crown\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Have you collected the components I require?","done":"From the materials you bring and from the scales of our fallen Qiraji foes I make you these pauldrons, mortal. May they grant you the protection you need and may the sight of them strike fear into our enemies.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Alliance Class Paladin Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8628\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Avenger's Crown this quest\nBring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Crystal Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8708":{"id":8708,"t":"Mace of Unending Life","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Ornate Hilt, 2 Jasper Idols, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Stone Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Ornate Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Jasper Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nMace of Unending Life\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"1028":{"id":1028,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":28,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the hidden shrine and re-enchant Dartol's Rod.\nReconstructed Rod\nProvided: Reconstructed Rod","desc":"Here is the completed rod, ‹name›. Reconstructing it was simple... it's finding the shrine that has the power to recharge it that will be the hard part.\nWith some focus and effort it shouldn't be too hard for someone like you, who's already accomplished so much.\nHead southeast of here--there are very few paths, so be careful--and keep your eyes to the north. The shrine is hidden within the mountains that surround this glade.\nOnce there, place the rod within the shrine... the rest is magic. Hehe.","rew":"You will receive:\nDartol's Rod of Transformation\nExperience: 1,700\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You can sense a subtle yet powerful force within the shrine and surrounding trees.\nYou begin placing the rod within the shrine and a soft thrumming noise emits from around you as the shrine begins to glow...","done":"After the glow dies, you can see the re-enchanted rod within the shrine's basin.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":53.5,"y":46.2,"n":"Shael'dryn","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":56.4,"y":49.2,"n":"Hidden Shrine","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3508":{"id":3508,"t":"Breaking the Ward","lv":58,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Loramus to complete the enlightenment spell.","desc":"You are foolhardy, ‹name›. It is an admirable quality of your kind - to blindly enter battle when you have little to no chance of success. I will assist you, if only to see just one of Razelikh's minions fall.\nTo break the ward placed over Razelikh's subordinates will take time and require the acquisition of rare artifacts.\nBe still, I must first perform the enlightenment ritual. The information I gather will assist me in forging weapons of great power.","rew":"Experience: 3,100","done":"The name of the beast must be found.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":60.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Loramus Thalipedes","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"708":{"id":708,"t":"The Black Box","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Corroded Black Box to the Hall of Arms in Ironforge.\nCorroded Black Box\nProvided: Corroded Black Box","desc":"The surface of this metallic black box is heavily pitted, as if it had been immersed in acid - it must have been sitting in the giant condor's stomach for a long time.\nTurning the box over, a symbol is found stamped on its bottom. Below the symbol are the words:\n\"Engine #19 - Ironforge Siege Brigade\"","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.8,"y":36.2,"n":"Pilot Longbeard","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"4788":{"id":4788,"t":"The Final Tablets","lv":58,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Fifth and Sixth Mosh'aru Tablets to Prospector Ironboot in Tanaris.\nFifth Mosh'aru Tablet Fifth Mosh'aru Tablet\nSixth Mosh'aru Tablet Sixth Mosh'aru Tablet","desc":"While I look over the third and fourth tablets of Mosh'aru, you must find the fifth and sixth! It will not be easy, for they are held by the Smolderthorn trolls within Blackrock Spire. The spire is a dark mountain of fire between the Burning Steppes and the Searing Gorge.\nGood luck, ‹name›. Blackrock Spire is no place for decent folk...","rew":"Experience: 7,750","back":"Have you been to the spire, ‹name›? Do you have the fifth and sixth tables?","done":"Unbelievable! You found them! You truly are a hero, ‹name›!\nThat's a good thing, because I've been reading the tablets you brought me before, and from what I gathered... we're going to need a hero to stop what's coming...","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":66.9,"y":24,"n":"Prospector Ironboot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"97908":{"id":97908,"t":"Camping 101 skinning","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Thuwd in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your skinning skill to 20","desc":"Being able to skillfully harvest the skins and hides of fallen beasts is one of the more valuable skills an adventurer can possess.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Camp Chair for your camp. Sometimes it's important to just take a load off, and you can use some of those hides you've gathered to make a comfy chair to sit in. A bit of relaxation can help ensure that you are at your peak condition and can strike where it counts the next time you find yourself in a dust-up.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Camp Chair. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.2,"y":45.2,"n":"Thuwd","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96628":{"id":96628,"t":"The adventurer","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Supply Bundle to Eric Brighthammer near Kharanos.\nProvided: Supply Bundle","desc":"Wait, ‹name›. I have another ask of you, before you brave that tunnel.\nMy mountaineers have reported an adventurer that's shown up just outside of Kharanos. Could you deliver these supplies to him?","back":"Are you here to learn about camping in the wilderness?","done":"You say these are from the mountaineers? Aye, I could use them. Thank you, ‹class›.\nHey, you've got the look of an adventurer yourself. How would you like to learn about camping?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":33.4,"y":71.8,"n":"Mountaineer Thalos","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94308":{"id":94308,"t":"Craftsmans writ enchanted mageweave pouch","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Enchanted Mageweave Pouch\nEnchanted Mageweave Pouch","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Enchanted Mageweave Pouch, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Enchanted Mageweave Pouch Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94308","cats":["crafting"]},"94228":{"id":94228,"t":"Craftsmans writ green iron boots","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Green Iron Boots\nGreen Iron Boots","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Green Iron Boots, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Please tell me you're the one with the boots...","done":"At last! I've been stomping around the wetlands with soggy feet for days!\nHopefully these aren't prone to rusting either. I trust you know what you're doing.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":50.1,"y":37.7,"n":"Kixxle","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"948":{"id":948,"t":"Onu","lv":17,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Onu at the Grove of the Ancients.","desc":"Onu, an Ancient of Lore at the Grove of the Ancients, knows of your journey to Cliffwater Falls and wishes to speak with you. The grove lies to the south, nestled near the mountains.\nThe Ancients are patient and wise, ‹name›. But if Onu seeks your counsel concerning what you saw in the falls, then I fear it is urgent.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"‹name›. You are here.\nGood.\nWe have matters...to discuss. You and I.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.3,"y":43.6,"n":"Barithras Moonshade","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.3,"n":"Onu","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"8948":{"id":8948,"t":"Anthion's Old Friend","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the incomplete Banner of Provocation to Falrin Treeshaper at the library in Dire Maul.\nIncomplete Banner of Provocation\nProvided: Incomplete Banner of Provocation","desc":"Theldren is not one to willingly participate in a fair fight. I've shaped this banner to display his family colors.\nWith some additional sorcery, this banner shall provoke him in a way he won't be able to resist.\nAn old acquaintance of mine named Falrin knows the exact procedure required. He has a particular way of... aggravating people. You shall find him at the library in Dire Maul.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Speak up stranger, can't you see I'm busy?","done":"Anthion sent you, you say? I thought he was dead. I guess I've heard stranger things in my life.\nVery well, then. What is it you want me to do with this banner?","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"7508":{"id":7508,"t":"The Forging of Quel'Serrar","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give the Dull and Flat Elven Blade to Lorekeeper Lydros.\nA Dull and Flat Elven Blade\nProvided: A Dull and Flat Elven Blade","desc":"If you wish to take on this task, present Lydros with the dull blade.","rew":"Experience: 7,050","back":"Excellent, let us begin...","done":"If you manage to enter the lair of the dragon, heat the blade under her fiery breath, and ultimately temper it in her blood, I shall bind the blade for your use.\nStart an item: A Dull and Flat Elven Blade End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7508\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 60, 26,950 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Foror's Compendium\nReturn Foror's Compendium of Dragon Slaying to the Athenaeum.\nNostro's Compendium of Dragon Slaying\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Forging of Quel'Serrar this quest\nGive the Dull and Flat Elven Blade to Lorekeeper Lydros.\nA Dull and Flat Elven Blade\n7,050 XP\n3 [ 60 ] The Forging of Quel'Serrar\nYou must get Onyxia to breathe fire on the Unfired Ancient Blade.\nLorekeeper Lydros\n9,950 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"308":{"id":308,"t":"Distracting Jarven","lv":7,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Thunder Ale sold by Innkeeper Belm , sold by Yanni Stoutheart , sold by Innkeeper Thulfram","back":"Hmph! There is all this booze down here. but I have strict orders not to touch it. If only I could get a taste of some of our Thunder Ale...that would sharpen my wits, no lying!","done":"For me? You're a true hero, ‹name›!\nDun Morogh The Hinterlands Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.6,"y":52.7,"n":"Jarven Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"788":{"id":788,"t":"Cutting Teeth","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Mottled Boars then return to Gornek at the Den.\nMottled Boar slain : 0/ 10","desc":"The first order of business will be to put a little strength in your backbone. I could send you out to the Barrens to hunt kodo, but well, in all honesty, you're more useful to us alive than dead.\nI believe you would find a good match with the mottled boars you'll find to the north of here.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSoft Wool Boots Battleworn Leather Gloves\nExperience: 170\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I hope you haven't returned to try and convince me that you have completed your task, ‹name›? No, of course not. I would think better of you.","done":"Hmmm, not bad, ‹name›. But don't let it get to your head...you'll fight tougher than boars in your career.\nNonetheless, you've proven yourself well, and your next trial will be against a considerably more dangerous opponent, so you'll need some extra protection.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.1,"y":68.3,"n":"Gornek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"148":{"id":148,"t":"Supplies from Darkshire","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Madame Eva.","desc":"Oh, what is a poor old man to do? I need some supplies from Darkshire, but the village is so far away and I am so old and feeble...I would never make the trip.\nCan you go to Darkshire and bring me back some Ghost Hair Thread? You can get it from Madame Eva at her home on the Darkshire square.","rew":"Experience: 490","done":"Ah, Ghost Hair Thread is what you need, is it? I'm afraid I have none in stock, but I can make some for you...if you can supply the ghost hair.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"68":{"id":68,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Dusty Unsent Letter to Clerk Daltry.\nA Dusty Unsent Letter\nProvided: A Dusty Unsent Letter","desc":"You find a Dusty Unsent Letter in the old footlocker.","rew":"Experience: 1,700\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ah, I remember you. You're the one who was asking about that Stalvan fellow. Did you ever find what you were looking for?","done":"Interesting. So the chap did spend some time in Moonbrook after all. It is rather odd the letter never got delivered. Nonetheless, I shall update the registry.\nWestfall Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":41.5,"y":66.7,"n":"Old Footlocker","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"228":{"id":228,"t":"Mor'Ladim","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 35s instead of 25s.","obj":"Kill Mor'Ladim, then return his skull to Commander Althea Ebonlocke in Darkshire.\nMor'Ladim's Skull Mor'Ladim","desc":"From what my scouts tell me, Mor'Ladim wanders throughout Duskwood, following a strange and meandering path through the cemetery. We buried him out past the house on the hill, you know where that is?\nThere isn't anything I can do to help you, but I wish you good luck.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I don't blame you if you're having trouble with him, ‹name›. Some of our strongest Watchers have been lost to Mor'Ladim.","done":"You killed him? That's no small accomplishment, ‹name›! On behalf of the people of Darkshire and the Night Watch, I thank you.\nAh... there is one small matter, however...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1268":{"id":1268,"t":"Suspicious Hoofprints","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report about the suspicious prints at the Shady Rest Inn to Krog in Brackenwall Village.","desc":"Rows of hoofprints lead away from the still-smoking skeleton of the Shady Rest Inn. There are at least a few visible impressions, with more rows of prints almost imperceptible in the soft mud of the marsh.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"Hoofprints... It could have been the quilboar, I suppose. Or maybe even the centaur. Their presence in the Barrens is not insignificant, and I would not think it a stretch to commit such an act.\nDid I tell you? It wasn't just that the inn was burned down... The owner's woman and pup were killed. Bad business, that.\nNonetheless, I will send Kagoro to find where the tracks lead.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":29.7,"y":47.6,"n":"Suspicious Hoofprint","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Krog","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5508":{"id":5508,"t":"Corruptor's Scourgestones","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Corruptor's Scourgestone Darkmaster Gandling , Marduk Blackpool in Scholomance , Hed'mush the Rotting , Lord Darkscythe and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nArgent Dawn Valor Token\nExperience: 550\n+25 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"A Corruptor's Scourgestone is the insignia of the Scourge's overlords. A powerful being that holds a position of authority over the Scourge will always possess one. To slay such a malevolent creature would surely advance the cause of the Argent Dawn, and all good causes!\nOn behalf of the Argent Dawn, I will give you a valor token in exchange for just a single one of these insignia. Use caution in acquiring one, ‹name› - such powerful beings are not to be trifled with.","done":"Congratulations, ‹name› - I am pleased to award you with an Argent Dawn valor token!\nTo acquire a valor token in such a manner indicates that you are a true hero in the cause of good. We value all effort brought to bear against the Scourge, but to take down one of their leaders is to truly deliver onto them a crushing defeat!\nFor the Dawn, my brother/sister!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9188":{"id":9188,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Brightcloth Pants","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 6 Brightcloth Pants and the Craftsman's Writ - Brightcloth Pants - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Brightcloth Pants\n6 Brightcloth Pants\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Brightcloth Pants","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order TR-95:\n6 Brightcloth Pants.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"I can almost see my reflection in these things! That's crazy.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6148":{"id":6148,"t":"The Scarlet Oracle, Demetria","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"The Scarlet Crusade is on the move. Somewhere along the road from Tyr's Hand to Stratholme you will find the Oracle, Demetria, and her entourage. Hunt her down and slay her. Return to Nathanos Blightcaller should you succeed.\nDemetria slain","desc":"Demetria is chief advisor to the Grand Crusader. She is called the Oracle due to her 'otherworldly' senses. She has successfully assisted the Crusade in several of their victories against the Scourge.\nWhile this ruse was successful in exposing her, if she truly does possess psychic powers, she will undoubtedly be expecting some sort of trouble. You are going to provide that 'trouble.'\nTrack down the Oracle and terminate her. They should be moving out of Tyr's Hand as we speak. Make me proud, worm.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGorewood Bow Stormrager Sacred Protector\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"What is your status, ‹name›?","done":"They will be reeling from this blow for years! Well done, ‹name›! You have earned not only my respect but also this reward.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"8228":{"id":8228,"t":"Could I get a Fishing Flier?","lv":60,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 55.","rew":"You will receive:\nFishing Tournament!","done":"There be a Fishin Contest in Booty Bay this Sunday! Here are the rules for ya!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.6,"y":33.1,"n":"Barrus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"3108":{"id":3108,"t":"Etched Rune","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Etched Rune and speak to Thorgas Grimson in Coldridge Valley.\nEtched Rune\nProvided: Etched Rune","desc":"While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the hunter trainer Thorgas. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Ya made it! Good to hear! Betcha didn't have to track me to find the place either. Haha!\nOur profession is pretty steeped in tradition, ‹name›. Learning the ways of the land. Learning to track a bear through the mountains. Even just surviving on wits alone takes a great deal of courage and cunning. Think you're capable?","done":"One thing you should always remember is that you gotta respect the world you're livin' in. The beasts that choose to fight along side you; the shine of your weapon; the weight of your ammo; the bite of a bitter wind; all these things you need to know intimately.\nI'll do what I can to help you, but most of the work's up to you. Anytime you think you're ready, come back and talk to me. I'll train you when I can.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.2,"y":67.5,"n":"Thorgas Grimson","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"6068":{"id":6068,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Thotar at Razor Hill.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Thotar at Razor Hill. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, it is time for you to begin your training.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Jen'shan","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":51.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Thotar","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"2948":{"id":2948,"t":"Gnome Improvement","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -1g -30s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring the Brilliant Gold Ring, a Silver Bar, a Moss Agate, and 30 silver coins to Talvash del Kissel in Ironforge.\nBrilliant Gold Ring\nSilver Bar Tattered Chest 9 % , Battered Chest 9 % , Tattered Chest 3 % , Battered Chest 0 % and 4 more\nMoss Agate Tink Sprocketwhistle 25 % , Greater Healing Ward 11.1 % , Tattered Chest 5 % , Venture Co. Drone 4.3 % and 4 more\nProvided: Brilliant Gold Ring","desc":"Listen ‹name›, that ring is yours, sure... but I can make you a better one! That design, like I said, is really simple. I am a lot more skilled now, and for the mere fee of thirty silver coins I'll spruce it up for you! Well, a little more than thirty, actually...\nI'm in a tight spot right now; all my material stock is all dried up. If you bring me a bar of silver and a moss agate, I'll add a silver and agate lattice to the ring that will give it a little more pizzazz!\nTrust me!","rew":"You will receive:\nTalvash's Gold Ring\nExperience: 2,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Do you have the materials I need? I wouldn't ask you for them if I wasn't down on my luck...","done":"Ah, exactly what I needed! Someday, when I find myself out of this hole that I am unjustly in, I will make for you, for EVERYONE the finest trinkets in all of Azeroth! Until then, thanks for being a sport about the reagents. I'd normally charge ten times what I have charged you for a ring of this quality...\nSpeaking of rings, here's your new one!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"6388":{"id":6388,"t":"Gryth Thurden","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Honorary Picks to Gryth Thurden in Ironforge.\nHonorary Picks\nProvided: Honorary Picks","desc":"Here are the honorary picks for Brock's students. If you've already been to Thelsamar, then you should fly a gryphon back there!\nTake the picks to our gryphon master, Gryth Thurden, and speak with him about a ride back to Thelsamar.","rew":"Experience: 210\n+25 reputation with Ironforge\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"You look like you have somewhere to go. Need one of my gryphons?","done":"You have to get these to Thelsamar, eh? That won't be a problem. As long as you've already been to Thelsamar and spoken to Thorgrum Borrelson, then you can take one of my gryphons back to him.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.4,"y":25.3,"n":"Golnir Bouldertoe","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60,"y":28.8,"n":"Gryth Thurden","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8868":{"id":8868,"t":"Elune's Blessing","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 90s instead of 0.","obj":"Summon Omen, defeat him and gain Elune's Blessing. Return to Valadar Starsong in Nighthaven","desc":"The beast Omen was once a hero of this world. A wolf of great strength and fortune, Omen fought beside the heroes of the War of the Ancients until he succumbed to demonic magics. Turning against his allies, he raged across Azeroth and carried death and terror in his wake.\nFinally defeated here, in Moonglade, Omen now sleeps among the silt of Lake Elune'ara. But each new year, during the festival, he stirs...\nGather cohorts, ‹name›, and summon and defeat the beast Omen. Earn the blessing of Elune!","rew":"You will receive:\nElune's Lantern Lunar Festival Fireworks Pack 3 Solid Stone\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Very well done, ‹name›. Defeating Omen sent his spirit back to the waters of Elune'ara. Although the beast himself is blessed by Elune and so cannot die, his anger will subside for another year.\nYour victory is a celebration, ‹name›--a celebration of the might of Omen, of you and your allies, and of the peace you have given this tragic hero of our past.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.7,"y":35.3,"n":"Valadar Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"7028":{"id":7028,"t":"Twisted Evils","lv":47,"min":41,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 15 Theradric Crystal Carvings for Willow in Desolace.\n15 Theradric Crystal Carving Kolk 80 % , Gelk 80 % , Magra 80 % , Maraudos 80 % and 4 more","desc":"The crystal caverns of Terramok lie to the west, deep within Maraudon... It is an ancient place with much history. And I am looking to get my hands on some of it, ‹class›. Relics of the old gods lie hidden behind the giant doors.\nIf you are willing to brave the twisted evils found in Maraudon, I believe I can make it worth your time. Collect the theradric crystal carvings you find, and return them to me.\nOnce I get the carvings, I will be able to... study them. These powers have been too long at rest...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAcumen Robes Sprightring Helm Relentless Chain Hulkstone Pauldrons\nExperience: 5,250","back":"Don't ask questions!\nYou have my request.","done":"Ha ha ha! I knew you'd be back.\n<Willow mutters>\n...So easy to convince.\n...Will do anything for the right price. Heh heh heh...\nDesolace Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":62.2,"y":39.6,"n":"Willow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"99108":{"id":99108,"t":"Sparring match","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat 3 other players in duels or Novice Warriors for Tang Stonehoof.\nPlayer Duels won or Novice Warriors defeated","desc":"Hail, young ‹class›. Though you are not a warrior and I cannot teach you that path, that does not mean you would not benefit from my tutelage.\nBefore you lies the arena. In it, it matters not who you call mother or whether you wield sword or bow. All are equal, and all learn to sharpen their horns in direct combat.\nWill you enter our space, and learn our ways for yourself? You may face any of these novices, or any other willing adversary. I care not which.","rew":"You will receive:\nMinor Healing Potion 3 Linen Bandage\nExperience: 550\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"You honor me with your abilities, ‹class›. Perhaps the new generation has hope yet.\nTake these to tend to your wounds, for many more battles await you in this harsh world.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":49.4,"y":60.4,"n":"Krang Stonehoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9108":{"id":9108,"t":"Plagueheart Gloves","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Gloves if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Gloves, 8 Wartorn Cloth Scraps and 4 Mooncloth.\nDesecrated Gloves\n8 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Mooncloth","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Gloves\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Gloves.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8388":{"id":8388,"t":"For Great Honor","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Alterac Valley Marks of Honor, 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor and 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Alterac Valley Mark of Honor\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Many brave fighters look up to you, ‹name›. You continue to be an example for all in the fight against the Alliance. What news do you bring from your journeys?","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+100 reputation with The Defilers","back":"Arathi is still wet with the blood of great warriors and the clash of steel still rings throughout Alterac. Do not waste my time unless you bring news from the front!","done":"You continue to honor the Horde, ‹name›. I'm glad to see you haven't turned soft.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8788":{"id":8788,"t":"A Gently Shaken Gift","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nDEPRECATED ITEM","done":"This present looks like it has been shaken a few times. The tag on it reads:\nTo a very special ‹race› ‹class›.\nDun Morogh Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.6,"n":"Gently Shaken Gift","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.3,"y":69.4,"n":"Gently Shaken Gift","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"9028":{"id":9028,"t":"The Source Revealed","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Apothecary Staffron Lerent in the Hillsbrad Foothills behind Ravenholdt Manor.","desc":"What? Treason? No, no. I assure you, my intentions are completely harmless.\nIs it so wrong to help those who wish to ease the painful ritual of courtship? Come, that is no crime.\nAnd to prove that I mean no harm, I will even tell you my source.\nThey were shipped to me by a Staffron Lerent, an apothecary of some sort. I never spoke with him.\nOur goblin middle man said that he worked in the foothills over Hillsbrad past that mysterious Ravenholdt Manor. I wish you luck in finding him.","done":"Yes, I made those fragrances. Wonderful smell, isn't it? Irresistible.\nOnce the warriors of Alliance and Horde alike are smitten with these feelings of love, they will be powerless to stop the rise of the Shadow Council.\nThey will be weakened, unprepared. As they worry for their loved ones, they will lose their edge.\nThe solution was so simple. Why did it take me so long to come upon it? The weakness of all is through the heart. And there is nothing you can do to stop the inevitable.\nStormwind City Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.8,"y":60.1,"n":"Evert Sorisam","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":89.5,"y":75.5,"n":"Apothecary Staffron Lerent","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94468":{"id":94468,"t":"Call of fire","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Torch of Eternal Flame to Bruegs Kindleborn in Dun Morogh.\nProvided: Torch of the Eternal Flame","desc":"Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Loch Modan. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.\nYou start off down the path back to Dun Morogh in search of Bruegs Kindleborn.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Totem Totem of Charged Flames\nExperience: 1,250","back":"Aye, Rhett? What do ye have there?","done":"By Madoran's beard, yer spirit burns brighter than any torch I've laid eyes on, Rhett--and that's somethin' to be proud of.\nKeep walkin' this path, and the elements'll bend to yer will. Our kin will come to ye for wisdom and guidance. So let me be the first to offer me hearty congratulations -- and present ye with yer newest totem. Ye've earned it, flameborn.\nDurotar Loch Modan Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":38.9,"y":58.2,"n":"Brazier of the Dormant Flame","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":31.9,"y":64.5,"n":"Brazier of the Dormant Flame","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":87.6,"y":43.6,"n":"Bruegs Kindleborn","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"7668":{"id":7668,"t":"The Darkreaver Menace","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Divination Scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement in the Scholomance. Doing so will bring forth spirits you must fight. Defeating these spirits will summon forth Death Knight Darkreaver; defeat him.\nBring Darkreaver's Head to Sagorne Creststrider in the Valley of Wisdom, Orgrimmar.\nDarkreaver's Head","desc":"Death Knight Darkreaver lords over the Great Ossuary in the Scholomance. He threatens to twist the spirit realm to do his own bidding, and he must be stopped! This is where the scryer you helped make comes into play.\nUse the divination scryer in the heart of the Great Ossuary's basement to call forth Darkreaver's spirit minions. Defeat the spirits and the death knight himself will appear. ‹name›, bring me his head! Only his demise will reverse the damage dome to the spirit realm!","rew":"You will receive:\nHelm of Latent Power\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Horde","back":"Time is critical, ‹name› - have you succeeded in stopping Death Knight Darkreaver's threat?","done":"This is a victory to savor, ‹name›! The demise of Darkreaver should restore the fragile fetters that anchor the spirit realm.\nYou have far exceeded what was asked of you, even when you had no notion of reward or compensation. You are truly a ‹class› of worth, my friend.\nI know that acting to preserve the spirit realm should be thanks enough, but please - accept this simple gift with my thanks.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.6,"y":36.2,"n":"Sagorne Creststrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93188":{"id":93188,"t":"Return to orgrul","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and report back to Orgrul near the northern entrance to Valley of Bones.\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"You have done enough on the front lines. We can handle ourselves.\nTell Orgrul that you have served your purpose. The Magram Front is stronger now, and we have our sights set on the outcast encampment as our next settlement when another fleet of fighters joins the fray.\nWell? Get going!\nLevel 43 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 39 41 46 54 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 93188\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat.\n3,600 XP\n11 [ 43 ] Long-Term Solutions\nM","cats":["shendralas"]},"8308":{"id":8308,"t":"Brann Bronzebeard's Lost Letter","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Brann Bronzebeard's Letter to Bronzebeard's Encampment in southern Silithus.\nBrann Bronzebeard's Lost Letter Hive'Ashi Ambusher 8.4 % , Hive'Ashi Drone 7.9 % , Hive'Regal Hive Lord 3.5 % , Hive'Regal Ambusher 3.2 % and 4 more\nProvided: Brann Bronzebeard's Lost Letter","desc":"To Whom It May Concern:\nIf you're reading this, I'm either dead or soon to be dead. It's hard to say. Most of the crew is dead anyhow.\nFound information about a Titan. Great battle between him and an Old God. Yes, a bona fide Old God. Found ancient tunnel leading to Ahn'Qiraj. Taking it.\nTake this letter to my old camp. Make sure my monkey is getting adequate food, water, and hugs.\n-Brann Bronzebeard, Explorer Extreme\nP.S. Watch out for crazy Old God worshipping night elf.","rew":"You will receive:\nBrann's Trusty Pick\nExperience: 8,300\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Oh dear.","done":"Well this explains a lot. If you ever find a way into Ahn'Qiraj, keep an eye out for ol' Brann. I'm afraid that he'll be powerless without his monkey.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":41.3,"y":88.5,"n":"Rutgar Glyphshaper","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8548":{"id":8548,"t":"Volunteer's Battlegear","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Cenarion Combat Badges, 3 Cenarion Logistics Badges and 7 Cenarion Tactical Badges to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also attain Friendly reputation with Cenarion Circle to be able to complete this quest.\n5 Cenarion Combat Badge\n3 Cenarion Logistics Badge\n7 Cenarion Tactical Badge\nReach 3000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The badges you collect from performing combat, logistics and tactical assignments for Cenarion Hold are more than just for show, ‹name›.\nYou'd be wise to hold on to them. As you prove your loyalty to our organization I can offer you some of the gear we reserve for our closest allies in exchange for those badges.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGloves of Earthen Power Band of Earthen Wrath Earthweave Cloak\nExperience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"It's in our best interest to keep our most loyal allies well geared, ‹name›.","done":"Great work, ‹name›. Please accept this on behalf of the Cenarion Circle. You've certainly earned it, friend!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Vargus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"78148":{"id":78148,"t":"Runes of the sorcerer kings","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Runes of the Sorcerer-Kings","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nRunes of the Sorcerer-Kings (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"6548":{"id":6548,"t":"Avenge My Village","lv":18,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Grimtotem Ruffians and 6 Grimtotem Mercenaries, and then return to Makaba Flathoof near the southeastern edge of Stonetalon.\nGrimtotem Ruffian slain : 0/ 8\nGrimtotem Mercenary slain : 0/ 6","desc":"The Grimtotem Clan raided my village and killed most everyone. I killed all I could, but barely escaped with my life.\n‹name›, all I wish now is that more of them are dead. You will find them just to the west of here.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Have you killed them yet?","done":"‹name›, I thank you... but I will never forget what the Grimtotem have done to my village.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.2,"y":27.8,"n":"Makaba Flathoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"628":{"id":628,"t":"Excelsior","lv":38,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Elder Crocolisk Skin to Drizzlik in Booty Bay.\nElder Crocolisk Skin Elder Saltwater Crocolisk 80 %","desc":"With the inside finished, all that's left is to add the outer layer. For this, I use only the best elder croc skins. They are more durable and a better canvas--if you will--for adding the designs and accents that make Drizzlik's Excelsior line.\nIt's hard to find that perfect skin though, the only one that fits my plan is the skin of an elder saltwater crocolisk. The elders only come out to defend the other saltwater crocs, so you might need to kill a few to draw one out.","rew":"You will receive:\nExcelsior Boots\nExperience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"I read somewhere that the saltwater crocilisks are slowly dying out... bad news for my business, isn't it?\nAnyways, I hope you have that elder saltwater crocolisk skin for me!","done":"Great! Thanks to your help I'll have this order filled and sent off to Director Riddlevox on the next boat to Undermine. Ahead of schedule, even!\nFor all your hard work, here, I made some extras, so take a pair. It's on Drizzlik.\nAnd remember, there's no boot so fine as one of Drizzlik's Excelsior line!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.3,"y":77.6,"n":"Drizzlik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"95748":{"id":95748,"t":"The gurubashi legends of old","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the hide and charcoal to create a rubbing of the Third Troll Legend tablet.\nThe Third Troll Legend","desc":"This is odd. This piece of the tablet you have brought me refers to the lost city of I'lalai as if it is a massive sprawling civilization. But the ruins off of the reef are not large enough to be something of that size.\n‹name›, to the north of the Vile Reef there is an ancient troll ruin on the hills along the coast. A tablet that contains legends of the lost troll city is within. I wish to study this legend further.\nTake this hide and charcoal to create a rubbing of this tablet, then return to me.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar\nLevel 40 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 36 38 43 51 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 95748","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"7908":{"id":7908,"t":"Arena master","lv":55,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Short John Mithril in the Stranglethorn Arena.\nArena Master","desc":"There must be more to being a master of the arena than this! Perhaps the Pirate who runs the event at Gurubashi will know!\nLevel 55 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 51 53 58 Side Both factions Type PvP Quest ID 7908","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8068":{"id":8068,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Illusionist's Mantle","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Al'tabim the All-Seeing a Primal Hakkari Shawl. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nAl'tabim the All-Seeing is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Shawl\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Magic is a raw, primal force to be shaped by those strong enough to do it. Mojo is our extension of this power; one such potent manipulation of it is in the form of illusion. How can one truly hope to win against a foe that is not even really there? We Zandalar know the power of this, and as such illusionists hold a honored place within the tribe.\nTake the needed Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub - for this, honor from the tribe and a powerful mantle used by our best illusionists will be yours!","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Illusionist's Mantle\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"How was your foray into Zul'Gurub? Did you drive your enemies mad through the power of illusion? Illusion or not, their deaths - and the Paragons of Power taken from them - will help thwart the rise of Hakkar.","done":"Success! You shall be honored in the tribe from here on! Zul'Gurub has certainly tasted the might of the Zandalar today, thanks to you ‹name›.\nWith the tribe's blessing, take the Zandalar illusionist's mantle. May it serve you well.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1428":{"id":1428,"t":"Continued Threat","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Marsh Inkspewers, 10 Marsh Flesheaters, and 10 Marsh Oracles, then return to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nMarsh Inkspewer slain : 0/ 10\nMarsh Flesheater slain : 0/ 10\nMarsh Oracle slain : 0/ 10","desc":"It pleases me to see your hatred for the fish men grows with mine.\nFind more of their kind along the beach, and when you've had your fill of combat, return to me. We shall speak then of a reward for your diligence.","rew":"Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Not until the sea and all her children are silenced will I be pleased... especially those disgusting fish men.","done":"Well done, ‹class›. I call for more of their blood. Let all the fish men perish.\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":83.8,"y":80.4,"n":"Katar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"9268":{"id":9268,"t":"War at Sea","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"40 Mageweave Cloth Northshire Guard 54.5 % , Deep Dweller 48.4 % , Refuge Pointe Defender 40.7 % , Stonard Hunter 40.2 % and 4 more\n4 Strong Flux Dalaran Miner , Tink Sprocketwhistle 0 % , Myolor Sunderfury 0 % , sold by Karm Ironquill and 4 more","back":"You seek to befriend the goblins of Tanaris once again, ‹name›? We're in need of materials for sails and guns to fight off our old enemies, the Bloodsail Buccaneers. Bring me mageweave and strong flux and we'll be on our way to pardoning your trespasses.","done":"Keep it coming, ‹name›. Us goblins don't forget that easily!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.4,"y":26.2,"n":"Rumsen Fizzlebrack","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"95508":{"id":95508,"t":"Unwelcome guests","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Help Walton survive the encounter with Terry Longdrink and the Kul Tiras marines.\nAssist Walton","desc":"Yes, I used to be a member of the Kul Tiras navy. After Lord Admiral took Theramore and started his campaign in Durotar, I had... \"objections\" to his methods. Particularly the methods involving executing civilians.\nThere's more to the story but... wait... what's that?\nThere's a group of men coming up the ridge!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nKeen Skinning Knife Wildgore Greatsword Walton's Second-Favorite Gun\nExperience: 1,000\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Well, looks like we are all alive. I... knew that someday that would catch up to me. I'm in your debt for your help here today.\nPlease, take this. It's not much, but its the least I can do.\nSafe travels, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":42,"y":11.4,"n":"Walton","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"868":{"id":868,"t":"Egg Hunt","lv":22,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Silithid Eggs and the Digging Claw to Korran at the Crossroads.\n12 Silithid Egg Silithid Mound , Silithid Creeper 80 % , Silithid Grub 80 % , Silithid Swarmer 80 % and 1 more\nDigging Claw\nProvided: Digging Claw","desc":"Hey, ‹name›. I been sent to the Crossroads to watch over the land and take note of its happenings for my masters in Orgrimmar.\nOne object of my studies are the insect-like creatures found to the south in the Field of Giants. We know little of the creatures, so I be makin' it a point to discover more. They seem to have intelligence to them, more so than any normal animal.\nTake this digging claw and collect some of the creatures' eggs from their mounds, but be careful: if alerted, they will attack you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHarlequin Robes Violet Scale Armor\nExperience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Be careful with the eggs you find, ‹name›. If they break, they be no good to me.","done":"You please me, ‹name›. The eggs and the tool. Well done.\nAnd for your reward...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.1,"y":29.6,"n":"Korran","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"7828":{"id":7828,"t":"Stalking the Stalkers","lv":48,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Markhor at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to kill 10 Silvermane Stalkers and 10 Silvermane Howlers. Return to him once the task is complete.\nMarkhor mentioned that the wolves hide in the wilds of the Hinterlands.\nSilvermane Stalker slain : 0/ 10\nSilvermane Howler slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Many brave trolls have been lost to the harsh wilds of the Hinterlands, ‹race›. The Silvermane wolves are one of the biggest threats to our hunters. They lay in wait, hiding amongst the bushes and landscape, then strike out when the opportunity presents itself.\nThis type of ferocity will not go unchecked!\nYou must think like the Silvermane. Stalk the stalkers! Slay them all!","rew":"Money: 1 40 1 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"Show them the might of Revantusk!","done":"A job well done, ‹race›. The Revantusk thank you for your contribution.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.2,"y":79.5,"n":"Huntsman Markhor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"388":{"id":388,"t":"The Color of Blood","lv":26,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 40s instead of 60s. Gives 5,550 experience instead of 2,650, 2.09 times as much. Partly read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a n","obj":"Nikova Raskol of Stormwind wants you to collect 10 Red Wool Bandanas.\n10 Red Wool Bandana Bruegal Ironknuckle 80 % , Bazil Thredd 80 % , Defias Insurgent 80 % , Defias Convict 80 % and 4 more","desc":"Bitterness flows through my veins like a cold river. My grandson, Mac, was such a good boy. A mere 14 years old. When the army was sent off to the front, Mac took up arms to defend the city. He was a guard in The Stockade, where the Defias gang is locked up. Mac reprimanded some of the prisoners for tearing their wool blankets to make scarves, a symbol of their gang. For that Mac was stabbed in the back.\nI want revenge. Bring me 10 of their precious Wool Bandanas. They are the color of blood.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,550\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I see you are back, ‹class›. Have you collected 10 Red Wool Bandanas from those Defias Scum in The Stockade yet?","done":"So these bandanas -- filthy tokens of corruption -- are what my Mac had to die for? Such a waste. Such a tragic sacrifice.\nBut alas, I cannot return to the past. Just know, ‹name›, that you have brought my family justice through your deeds.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":76.5,"y":63.7,"n":"Nikova Raskol","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-stockade"]},"6628":{"id":6628,"t":"Test of Lore","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Answer Parqual Fintallas' question successfully and then speak to him again. He will remain in the Undercity until you are ready.","desc":"So the time is once again upon us. As a student of lore, you have shown great tenacity by undertaking my task.\nAnd so now I offer you your question. If you are ready, speak to me again, and take all the time you need, ‹name›--there is no pressure to answer quickly.","rew":"Experience: 250","back":"There is only one rule I feel you must know if you wish to survive in this world: the more you know, the more you'll see.\nIf you study, if you observe, then you will begin to see things in the world that no other ‹race› will see.","done":"Well done, ‹name›. I had my doubts if you studied the text I asked you to get, but you've answered correctly.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":57.8,"y":65.4,"n":"Parqual Fintallas","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1108":{"id":1108,"t":"Indurium","lv":39,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Indurium Flakes to Martek the Exiled in the Badlands.\n10 Indurium Flake Stonevault Basher 60 % , Stonevault Cave Hunter 60 % , Stonevault Rockchewer 60 % , Stonevault Shaman 60 % and 2 more","desc":"I'm not out here just to stay away from people. There is a wealth of metal in the Badlands, ‹name›, if you have the guts to get it.\nThe metal's called indurium and as luck would have it, it is rumored to possess high resistance to heat and stress. It might work for Fizzle's car.\nBut let's make sure. Get me samples of indurium and I'll test its properties.\nTrue indurium ore lies deep in Uldaman, but the Stonevault troggs of the Badlands sometimes have flakes of it on them. Bring me those flakes.","rew":"Experience: 3,000","back":"Did you find any indurium flakes, ‹name›. I have my forge heated up and ready to test them.","done":"Ah yes, these will do fine. Now let's put them in some heat and see how they fare...","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":42.2,"y":52.7,"n":"Martek the Exiled","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1188":{"id":1188,"t":"Safety First","lv":41,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Seaforium Booster to Shreev in Gadgetzan.\nSeaforium Booster Gizmorium Shipping Crate\nProvided: Seaforium Booster","desc":"But wait, what's this? Shreev left the safety on. That will limit the amount of power I can draw from the booster at any time. I told him I wanted it off! This is no good.\nYou have to take this to the Gadgetzan Gizmorium in the Tanaris Desert and have Shreev remove this.","rew":"Experience: 825\n+25 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"As I'm sure you know, the Gizmorium can service all of your tinkering needs! How can I help you?","done":"Only Razzeric would take a look at this and say that I'd somehow put some sort of safety lock on it. This booster is almost completely seaforium explosives. I already modified it so that more of its payload would be delivered upon use, but Razzeric is never content unless he goes to eleven!\nThousand Needles Tanaris Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.3,"y":76.1,"n":"Razzeric","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":51,"y":27.2,"n":"Shreev","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"3908":{"id":3908,"t":"It's a Secret to Everybody","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Linken's Sword to Donova Snowden in Winterspring.\nLinken's Training Sword\nProvided: Linken's Training Sword","desc":"You see, I have no idea how I ended up here. No one really knows -- it's a secret to everybody! I just can't seem to remember anything...\nThese items you brought to me, though... I am remembering something.\nMy sword. I am supposed to strengthen it somehow, but I'm really not sure why. Sorry I can't tell you more, but I just don't remember!\nAnyhoo, I do know where you can take it -- Donova Snowden in Winterspring. You'll find her by the hot springs. She can temper the sword by the pools there.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"My, my... So Linken did finally get around to sending me his sword.","done":"Well, of course I can temper this sword. While I'm working, you can explain what took Linken so long to get this to me. He's not usually one to forget things...\nUn'Goro Crater Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":44.7,"y":8.1,"n":"Linken","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":31.3,"y":45.2,"n":"Donova Snowden","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4148":{"id":4148,"t":"Bloodpetal Zapper","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bloodpetal Sprout Stone Guardian , Tar Creeper , Tar Lord , Tar Beast and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nBloodpetal Zapper\nMoney: 1 60 1 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,950","back":"For the zapper to work, it needs a sample of the target creature. Head out into the crater and collect a Bloodpetal sprout. Then I can calibrate it to work on Muigin's little friends...\nIf he weren't so stubborn, we could be on our way home, already... But until then, I'll just have to show him that his little prank doesn't bother me at all!","done":"Looks like this is going to work perfectly, ‹name›. Now remember, if you see any of those pests around, don't hesitate to use that zapper!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":45.5,"y":8.7,"n":"Larion","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1508":{"id":1508,"t":"Blind Cazul","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Zankaja in Orgrimmar.","desc":"Hmm... But, of course, that is not why you have come to speak with me.\nIf Gan'rul has sent you to me, it must be that you are to summon a succubus, and need an object to use for enticement.\nHmm... If you trust a blind man to lead you, ‹name›, then listen. In the bluffs of Orgrimmar, west of the wind rider tower, lives Zankaja. She waits for the return of her mate.\nGo to her.","rew":"Experience: 390","done":"Have you come with news of Dogran? He was to have returned days ago, and I have heard nothing...","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":47.1,"y":46.4,"n":"Cazul","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":37,"y":59.4,"n":"Zankaja","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"468":{"id":468,"t":"Report to Mountaineer Rockgar","lv":21,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mountaineer Rockgar.","desc":"Mountaineer Rockgar is looking for volunteers for a mission through Dun Algaz and into the Wetlands.\nIf you want to get your boots wet in that soggy county to the north, then speak with Rockgar at Dun Algaz. Dun Algaz is north up the road, beyond the guard tower.","rew":"Experience: 170\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Hello, ‹class›! You're here for the scouting mission, are you? Very good!\nI hope your gear is in good condition, because this \"scouting\" mission has changed into something more messy...","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":34.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Mountaineer Kadrell","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":25.4,"y":10.4,"n":"Mountaineer Rockgar","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92468":{"id":92468,"t":"Call of earth","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Rough Quartz to Windshaper Boros in Thendal Grove.\nProvided: Rough Quartz","desc":"Take this Rough Quartz from me and bring it to the one you call Windshaper Boro as proof of our meeting. He will craft a totem for you, and this shard will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast many others.\nBe patient, ‹name›. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what the elements ask of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarth Totem\nExperience: 360\n+50 reputation with Windshapers","back":"As you will come to learn, the path we walk is not as simple as it may seem. While we seek to find the voice needed to speak with the spirits of the winds, the winds are but one of the elemental forces of this world. Only through understanding, and--we hope--mastery of all four elements will we regain our voice to again sing the songs of the wind.","done":"Good!\nThe totem I will craft for you is more than a symbol of your status among ‹class›--it has abilities beyond that. One use of the totem is as a focus for spells. Those spells are tied to the earth, and as you earn greater and greater wisdom, more of the earth's abilities will be made accessible to you.\nThe trainers will know when you are ready for greater knowledge.\nBut for now, take this earth totem...","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":49.6,"y":24,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.8,"y":23.6,"n":"Windshaper Boro","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92708":{"id":92708,"t":"A grand adventure","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Listen to what Ayessa Dawnsinger has to say.\nListen to Ayessa","desc":"The Windshapers have been hard at work trying to respond to the current crisis on Zephras Isle. We have made several surprising discoveries in our search for the missing wind spirits, and we are developing a plan of action that could help us gain the means to save the island.\nWe'll need strong young adventurer's like yourself for this to work however. Please, if you have a moment, let us speak on this further.","done":"So now you see? There is a world of knowledge and untapped potential outside of Skywall. This will never stop being our home, but I've come to believe that the path to our salvation lies below. We must travel to Azeroth and gain the power and means to save Zephras Isle. This is the way.\nWill you have the courage to join us when the time comes?","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8148":{"id":8148,"t":"The Maelstrom's Wrath","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from The Maelstrom's Wrath. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Maelstrom's Tendril","rew":"You will receive:\nMaelstrom's Wrath\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Molthor delivers word from King Rastakhan, ‹name›. The royal court is most impressed with your decimation of the Hakkari forces. I am to award you with the final weave in your talisman. Hand it to me.","done":"Your journey has only just begun, young ‹class›. Perhaps one day you will visit the Maelstrom and glance into the heart of the world.\nI wish you power and fortitude!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});